{% comment %}
  cx-live — the single source of truth for "is Cellexia Reviews live on THIS
  request?" (SPEC-1.14 §3). Echoes exactly `1` (live here) or `0` (not).

  Decision, evaluated by Shopify's Liquid renderer with the request's real
  market context (localization.market.handle) — never client-side:

    1. `cellexia.live` metafield explicitly false        → 0 (live nowhere)
    2. `cellexia.live_markets.scope == "markets"`        → 1 only when this
       request's market handle is in `handles`, else 0
    3. anything else (absent metafield / scope "all" /
       malformed value)                                  → 1 when rule 1
       passed — the exact pre-1.14 behavior, so upgrades
       are shopper-invisible

  Consumers MUST render via capture and strip Shopify's app-snippet wrapper
  comments (SPEC-1.8 §5) before comparing:

    {%- capture cx_live_raw -%}{% render 'cx-live' %}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign cx_live_raw = cx_live_raw | remove: '<!-- BEGIN app snippet: cx-live -->' | remove: '<!-- END app snippet -->' | strip -%}

  A comparison against the UNstripped capture would read "not 1" everywhere
  and silently hide the app on every page — strip first, always.
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign cx_live_out = '1'
  if shop.metafields.cellexia.live.value == false
    assign cx_live_out = '0'
  else
    assign cx_lm = shop.metafields.cellexia.live_markets.value
    if cx_lm
      if cx_lm.scope == 'markets'
        assign cx_live_out = '0'
        assign cx_market_handle = ''
        if localization.market and localization.market.handle
          assign cx_market_handle = localization.market.handle | downcase
        endif
        if cx_market_handle != ''
          for cx_h in cx_lm.handles
            assign cx_h_norm = cx_h | downcase
            if cx_h_norm == cx_market_handle
              assign cx_live_out = '1'
            endif
          endfor
        endif
      elsif cx_lm.scope == 'all'
        assign cx_live_out = '1'
      else
        comment
          SPEC-1.14 §0.3: a PRESENT but unrecognized live_markets value
          (foreign write, corruption) fails CLOSED — not live anywhere.
          Only an ABSENT metafield keeps the pre-1.14 all-markets behavior.
        endcomment
        assign cx_live_out = '0'
      endif
    endif
  endif
  echo cx_live_out
-%}
